00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:22.980
before we start to create the art.

533
00:26:22.980 --> 00:26:25.640
And how could we use art as a vehicle

534
00:26:25.640 --> 00:26:29.570
of beauty being the first tenet of spirituality

535
00:26:29.570 --> 00:26:31.530
that can transform the planet,

536
00:26:31.530 --> 00:26:36.530
that can lift our experience of life here by healing us,

537
00:26:37.280 --> 00:26:41.850
by feeding us, by nourishing us?

538
00:26:41.850 --> 00:26:46.850
And she had a very visceral transcendental experience

539
00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:49.850
using the Water Tiger techniques.

540
00:26:49.850 --> 00:26:52.160
And she had a complete,

541
00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:55.110
she was given a body of work exactly the way it looks

542
00:26:55.110 --> 00:26:58.630
in exactly the format and the date

543
00:26:58.630 --> 00:27:01.640
that she needs to do it by and all these kind of things.

544
00:27:01.640 --> 00:27:05.570
And also, very connected to some deep suffering

545
00:27:05.570 --> 00:27:08.320
in her journey that she had to face.

546
00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:10.590
That was very probably the thing

547
00:27:10.590 --> 00:27:13.120
that was the hardest thing for her.

548
00:27:13.120 --> 00:27:17.610
In my work, the greatest treasure is in the trauma.

549
00:27:17.610 --> 00:27:18.910
And so, when I work with somebody,

550
00:27:18.910 --> 00:27:21.600
I'm looking for the thing they never told anybody.

551
00:27:21.600 --> 00:27:24.120
I may be the first person that they shared it with.

552
00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:28.200
Or the thing that is absolutely irreconcilable.

553
00:27:28.200 --> 00:27:31.930
And if I am lucky enough and blessed enough

554
00:27:31.930 --> 00:27:34.270
to serve my purpose,

555
00:27:34.270 --> 00:27:36.030
by the end of that session,

556
00:27:36.030 --> 00:27:39.340
they have a different perspective on the events.

557
00:27:39.340 --> 00:27:42.250
Right, and that tracks back to this idea

558
00:27:43.500 --> 00:27:46.010
that we began this conversation with,

559
00:27:46.010 --> 00:27:48.910
which is this thing where there's,

560
00:27:48.910 --> 00:27:50.900
everybody has something that they're hiding from

561
00:27:50.900 --> 00:27:52.380
or that they're hiding from the world

562
00:27:52.380 --> 00:27:55.090
or that they're hiding from themselves.

563
00:27:55.090 --> 00:27:57.460
And to the extent that you can muster the courage

564
00:27:57.460 --> 00:28:01.120
to actually look at that, to deconstruct that,

565
00:28:01.120 --> 00:28:05.200
and find the gem or the meaning or the beauty

566
00:28:05.200 --> 00:28:07.310
or the opportunity in that,

567
00:28:07.310 --> 00:28:11.260
that's where the crux of transformation begins.

568
00:28:11.260 --> 00:28:14.230
And this has always been your thing with me.

569
00:28:14.230 --> 00:28:15.590
And when we weathered

570
00:28:15.590 --> 00:28:17.790
all of our challenges and difficulties,

571
00:28:17.790 --> 00:28:19.680
it's like, how do we flip this

572
00:28:19.680 --> 00:28:23.890
and look at it from a perspective of opportunity

573
00:28:23.890 --> 00:28:25.270
rather than victimhood?

574
00:28:25.270 --> 00:28:26.697
Like, "Why is this happening to me?

575
00:28:26.697 --> 00:28:28.170
"Isn't this terrible?"

576
00:28:28.170 --> 00:28:31.550
Instead, like, "This is your divine moment."

577
00:28:31.550 --> 00:28:33.217
Like, "This is the opportunity

578
00:28:33.217 --> 00:28:34.990
"that you've been waiting for."

579
00:28:34.990 --> 00:28:37.450
And just that mental shift,

580
00:28:37.450 --> 00:28:39.590
as difficult as that might be

581
00:28:39.590 --> 00:28:43.870
or as counterintuitive or challenging

582
00:28:43.870 --> 00:28:46.810
to inhabit that in your body,

583
00:28:46.810 --> 00:28:50.510
I've found that to be incredibly powerful.

584
00:28:50.510 --> 00:28:53.330
I've seen you do that in the context of our family

585
00:28:53.330 --> 00:28:56.030
and I've seen you do that with so many other people.

586
00:28:56.030 --> 00:28:59.660
And it is maybe the hardest thing you'll ever do,

587
00:28:59.660 --> 00:29:03.400
but also carries that potential energy

588
00:29:03.400 --> 00:29:06.684
for the change that people are yearning for.

589
00:29:06.684 --> 00:29:07.767
Definitely.

590
00:29:09.280 --> 00:29:14.280
And "Let it be beautiful" is sort of one of my mantras.

591
00:29:14.490 --> 00:29:16.680
It's like, let it be beautiful, whatever,

592
00:29:16.680 --> 00:29:17.820
it may be scary.

593
00:29:17.820 --> 00:29:19.540
It's not autopilot.

594
00:29:19.540 --> 00:29:22.400
It's not acting like everything is the same.

595
00:29:22.400 --> 00:29:24.637
It's not getting to a place and saying,

596
00:29:24.637 --> 00:29:26.467
"We're here and now we're here,

597
00:29:26.467 --> 00:29:29.207
"and we're gonna be a static form

598
00:29:29.207 --> 00:29:31.750
"for the rest of our lives because we're here."

599
00:29:31.750 --> 00:29:32.910
Doesn't work that way.

600
00:29:32.910 --> 00:29:34.190
It's always changing.

601
00:29:34.190 --> 00:29:36.400
And no matter how difficult,

602
00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:37.820
whatever the evolution is,

603
00:29:37.820 --> 00:29:40.110
whatever needs to be looked at,

604
00:29:40.110 --> 00:29:42.060
it has to be beautiful.

605
00:29:42.060 --> 00:29:44.880
It has to be beautiful because life is divine.

606
00:29:44.880 --> 00:29:45.713
It's sacred.

607
00:29:45.713 --> 00:29:46.800
This is a privilege.

608
00:29:46.800 --> 00:29:50.220
It's a divine privilege to be in a body at this time.

609
00:29:50.220 --> 00:29:54.650
And we are co-creating our experience with our life.

610
00:29:54.650 --> 00:29:57.590
And so, rather than hide

611
00:29:59.060 --> 00:30:01.860
from what is bubbling inside of you

612
00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:05.910
or what is beckoning your attention,

613
00:30:05.910 --> 00:30:10.910
why not face it and communicate with it and exchange with it

614
00:30:10.930 --> 00:30:14.093
and create something beautiful from it?

615
00:30:15.510 --> 00:30:16.343
One of the things,

616
00:30:16.343 --> 00:30:18.090
and we've talked about this before,

617
00:30:20.230 --> 00:30:25.230
that I think is powerful but also challenging to me

618
00:30:26.410 --> 00:30:30.410
is this idea that you don't wanna rob someone

619
00:30:30.410 --> 00:30:32.460
of their divine moment, right?

620
00:30:32.460 --> 00:30:34.560
Like, if somebody's going through a hard time

621
00:30:34.560 --> 00:30:36.420
whether it's emotional or financial

622
00:30:36.420 --> 00:30:39.940
or maybe they've experienced the death of a loved one,

623
00:30:39.940 --> 00:30:42.050
or maybe they lost their job,

624
00:30:42.050 --> 00:30:42.960
they can't pay their bills.

625
00:30:42.960 --> 00:30:46.083
Whatever flavor that shows up in,

626
00:30:47.670 --> 00:30:49.000
the idea of,

627
00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:50.830
we have this urge like we wanna step in,

628
00:30:50.830 --> 00:30:52.390
we wanna intervene, we wanna help.

629
00:30:52.390 --> 00:30:54.060
We wanna alleviate the pain.

630
00:30:54.060 --> 00:30:56.300
We wanna solve the problem.

631
00:30:56.300 --> 00:31:00.630
But that's also the opportunity

632
00:31:01.740 --> 00:31:04.560
to step back and allow that person that experience

633
00:31:04.560 --> 00:31:08.040
because there's some lesson that needs to be learned

634
00:31:08.040 --> 00:31:10.840
as a result of running that gauntlet.

635
00:31:10.840 --> 00:31:13.053
And so, it's this tension between,

636
00:31:14.820 --> 00:31:18.160
it's a tension around, how do you best love somebody?

637
00:31:18.160 --> 00:31:19.850
Do you opt out?

638
00:31:19.850 --> 00:31:23.680
And is it more loving to let them have that experience

639
00:31:23.680 --> 00:31:24.880
without your interference?

640
00:31:24.880 --> 00:31:29.410
And at what point do you step in and try to course correct

641
00:31:29.410 --> 00:31:32.810
because you see something going horribly awry?

642
00:31:32.810 --> 00:31:35.375
I think this is a really good question.

643
00:31:35.375 --> 00:31:39.660
And for me, it's less about what you do

644
00:31:39.660 --> 00:31:43.040
and more about the energy with which

645
00:31:43.040 --> 00:31:44.933
you are viewing the individual.

646
00:31:47.350 --> 00:31:51.160
If my friend is bleeding,

647
00:31:51.160 --> 00:31:53.670
I'm gonna get them some bandages

648
00:31:53.670 --> 00:31:58.600
and I'm gonna clean them off and make them safe

649
00:31:58.600 --> 00:32:00.247
and get them food and be like,

650
00:32:00.247 --> 00:32:01.080
"Are you okay?

651
00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:01.913
"Like, you're good?

652
00:32:01.913 --> 00:32:02.767
"Like, I'm here."

653
00:32:03.880 --> 00:32:08.390
I think the real power is in how I'm viewing that person.

654
00:32:08.390 --> 00:32:12.640
Am I choosing to view that person as a casualty?

655
00:32:12.640 --> 00:32:16.960
Or let's say the person was irresponsible and created that.

656
00:32:16.960 --> 00:32:20.340
Let's say, I don't know what a good example.

657
00:32:20.340 --> 00:32:23.470
Let's say they caused that accident

658
00:32:23.470 --> 00:32:26.020
because they are using drugs

659
00:32:26.020 --> 00:32:29.593
and they got in a situation and the accident happened.

660
00:32:31.380 --> 00:32:34.480
I think as powerful healers and co-creators

661
00:32:34.480 --> 00:32:38.970
and beings of a version of a Christic form

662
00:32:38.970 --> 00:32:40.890
or what might be a Christ-embodied,

663
00:32:40.890 --> 00:32:42.930
free from religion, free from isms.

664
00:32:42.930 --> 00:32:46.530
Just from the very nature of being humane,

665
00:32:46.530 --> 00:32:48.053
of being human beings,

666
00:32:49.330 --> 00:32:51.470
we have the ability to hold that person

667
00:32:51.470 --> 00:32:54.050
in their highest vision and say:

668
00:32:54.050 --> 00:32:56.320
It's okay, man, you got this.

669
00:32:56.320 --> 00:32:57.403
I know you stumbled.

670
00:32:59.012 --> 00:33:01.830
I see you as such a beautiful being.

671
00:33:01.830 --> 00:33:04.860
You have so many amazing qualities.

672
00:33:04.860 --> 00:33:06.530
You know, I love this about you.

673
00:33:06.530 --> 00:33:08.340
I love that about you.

674
00:33:08.340 --> 00:33:09.970
And I know you're struggling

675
00:33:11.890 --> 00:33:14.710
and I'm not gonna solve your problem for you.

676
00:33:14.710 --> 00:33:17.970
I'm not going to intervene with my judgment.

677
00:33:17.970 --> 00:33:20.020
I'm just gonna hold you in love,

678
00:33:20.020 --> 00:33:25.020
knowing that this force, God, creation has you

679
00:33:25.410 --> 00:33:28.200
and that you're in your process.

680
00:33:28.200 --> 00:33:32.180
And how does that work for you with parenting?

681
00:33:32.180 --> 00:33:33.680
It gets a little bit trickier.

682
00:33:34.570 --> 00:33:35.403
Yeah, I mean,

683
00:33:35.403 --> 00:33:40.403
and this is a subject that is difficult to talk about

684
00:33:40.783 --> 00:33:43.557
because we actually don't have permission to talk about it.

685
00:33:43.557 --> 00:33:44.710
Right, we're not gonna talk about

686
00:33:44.710 --> 00:33:46.478
our kids specifically, but-

687
00:33:46.478 --> 00:33:47.651
It's the same thing-

688
00:33:47.651 --> 00:33:49.564
But the general idea of,

689
00:33:49.564 --> 00:33:51.610
when are you in the allowing,

690
00:33:51.610 --> 00:33:54.430
when are you in the, "I'm gonna intervene, here?"

691
00:33:54.430 --> 00:33:56.880
Well, trust me, I think it's a dance, right?

692
00:33:56.880 --> 00:33:59.740
And I mean, there's many times I'll just go in

693
00:33:59.740 --> 00:34:02.970
to check on them, to make sure they're there

694
00:34:02.970 --> 00:34:05.983
and they're not hurting themselves and they're fine.

695
00:34:08.590 --> 00:34:10.590
I trust my mother's intuition.

696
00:34:10.590 --> 00:34:12.620
I mean, trust me.

697
00:34:12.620 --> 00:34:14.620
A lot of people are considering,

698
00:34:14.620 --> 00:34:16.660
they have suicidal thoughts.

699
00:34:16.660 --> 00:34:18.320
Especially now, you know,

700
00:34:18.320 --> 00:34:20.430
and especially in our youth.

701
00:34:20.430 --> 00:34:22.860
So, I think you have to keep a close eye.

702
00:34:22.860 --> 00:34:26.940
But I think when you come into judgment

703
00:34:26.940 --> 00:34:30.063
thinking that that's gonna stop the action,

704
00:34:31.380 --> 00:34:34.650
nobody changes in a field of judgment.

705
00:34:34.650 --> 00:34:36.190
People change in a field

706
00:34:36.190 --> 00:34:38.740
of unconditional love and compassion.

707
00:34:38.740 --> 00:34:41.950
And that's not that hard with our kids

708
00:34:41.950 --> 00:34:45.250
because we all adore our kids.

709
00:34:45.250 --> 00:34:46.940
Right, but I think what is happening

710
00:34:46.940 --> 00:34:50.780
is everybody's under duress.

711
00:34:50.780 --> 00:34:53.480
The anxiety levels are through the roof.

712
00:34:53.480 --> 00:34:56.950
People's economic situations are being challenged.

713
00:34:56.950 --> 00:35:01.870
And so, parents are feeling a lot of anxiety

714
00:35:01.870 --> 00:35:04.470
disproportionate to what they're used to.

715
00:35:04.470 --> 00:35:08.890
And without a level, a deep level of awareness,

716
00:35:08.890 --> 00:35:12.340
it's very easy for that anxiety or stress

717
00:35:12.340 --> 00:35:14.280
to leak out onto the children.

718
00:35:14.280 --> 00:35:18.710
And the children are under their own level of duress

719
00:35:18.710 --> 00:35:21.490
with having to do their schooling from home.

720
00:35:21.490 --> 00:35:23.600
And it just becomes this soup

721
00:35:26.660 --> 00:35:31.220
of mental unfitness in which nobody's acting

722
00:35:31.220 --> 00:35:32.900
as well as they would like to act.

723
00:35:32.900 --> 00:35:37.630
And it creates a lot of chaos and problems.

724
00:35:37.630 --> 00:35:39.750
I think we're seeing this epidemic now

725
00:35:39.750 --> 00:35:43.940
of children struggling with how to navigate this world

726
00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:45.880
where their entire life is on screens

727
00:35:45.880 --> 00:35:48.280
and they can't see their friends or go to school.

728
00:35:48.280 --> 00:35:50.830
Parents who are under stress,

729
00:35:50.830 --> 00:35:53.690
they're not happy that their kids are in this situation

730
00:35:53.690 --> 00:35:54.900
and they're trying to work from home.

731
00:35:54.900 --> 00:35:57.610
All of these things are unprecedented

732
00:35:57.610 --> 00:35:59.160
and creating complications

733
00:35:59.160 --> 00:36:03.160
that we haven't developed tools for.

734
00:36:03.160 --> 00:36:04.180
Yeah, definitely.

735
00:36:04.180 --> 00:36:06.870
I mean, I would say there's always

736
00:36:06.870 --> 00:36:09.000
these opportunities in being a parent.

737
00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:11.860
It's like it's sort of part of the journey.

738
00:36:11.860 --> 00:36:14.690
There's gonna come a point where your child just cancels you

739
00:36:14.690 --> 00:36:18.883
and thinks you're completely outdated and irrelevant.

740
00:36:19.730 --> 00:36:20.563
That's part of the journey.

741
00:36:20.563 --> 00:36:21.396
I'm already there.

742
00:36:21.396 --> 00:36:23.191
Yeah, definitely, we're there.

743
00:36:23.191 --> 00:36:24.560
I always thought I was gonna be the cool dad.

744
00:36:24.560 --> 00:36:26.313
No, that's the illusion.

745
00:36:26.313 --> 00:36:27.900
That's the illusion.

746
00:36:27.900 --> 00:36:30.630
No one is the cool dad to their kids.

747
00:36:30.630 --> 00:36:32.083
No one is the cool mom.

748
00:36:33.679 --> 00:36:35.440
I mean, and I would say on the other side,

749
00:36:35.440 --> 00:36:38.300
there's a lot of benefits from being sequestered

750
00:36:38.300 --> 00:36:40.530
from quarantine that have,

751
00:36:40.530 --> 00:36:43.130
as I'm gonna say, added five years onto our lives.

752
00:36:43.130 --> 00:36:45.620
I mean, possibly saved our children's lives.

753
00:36:45.620 --> 00:36:46.540
Maybe it kept,

754
00:36:46.540 --> 00:36:49.460
maybe they're unhappy and they're kicking dirt,

755
00:36:49.460 --> 00:36:53.003
but they're in a more contained space than they would have.

756
00:36:55.650 --> 00:36:56.483
We aren't God.

757
00:36:56.483 --> 00:36:58.310
We can't see exactly what the journey is.

758
00:36:58.310 --> 00:37:00.860
But you know, listen.

759
00:37:00.860 --> 00:37:03.110
I think it's a great hilarity of the universe

760
00:37:03.110 --> 00:37:05.050
that as a mother,

761
00:37:05.050 --> 00:37:09.300
I give birth to a baby that needs me for every single thing,

762
00:37:09.300 --> 00:37:12.200
like it's this symbiotic union.

763
00:37:12.200 --> 00:37:13.490
And then at some point,

764
00:37:13.490 --> 00:37:15.970
that being grows up and is just like, "Fuck off!"

765
00:37:15.970 --> 00:37:18.987
I mean, it's kind of funny because you're just like,

766
00:37:18.987 --> 00:37:21.820
"What is going on here," you know?

767
00:37:21.820 --> 00:37:22.953
So, that's kind of, I think,

768
00:37:22.953 --> 00:37:24.380
a funny thing from the universe.

769
00:37:24.380 --> 00:37:26.330
But I think that in general,

770
00:37:26.330 --> 00:37:29.280
I think as a culture we hold our kids back too long.

771
00:37:29.280 --> 00:37:32.070
I think they should go into their own living spaces

772
00:37:32.070 --> 00:37:36.460
with communes at age 12, with their own bank accounts,

773
00:37:36.460 --> 00:37:41.010
and they should be treated as adults much sooner

774
00:37:41.010 --> 00:37:44.460
because there's so much turmoil between them

775
00:37:44.460 --> 00:37:46.830
still being in the house.

776
00:37:46.830 --> 00:37:49.520
And like I said, we're cool parents,

777
00:37:49.520 --> 00:37:51.370
and we have it, too.

778
00:37:51.370 --> 00:37:53.083
So, yeah.

779
00:37:55.730 --> 00:37:58.670
I think the unconditional love part, though,

780
00:37:58.670 --> 00:38:00.950
the more you can cultivate that within yourself,

781
00:38:00.950 --> 00:38:02.670
and let's be clear.

782
00:38:02.670 --> 00:38:05.330
It doesn't mean that you don't have preferences.

783
00:38:05.330 --> 00:38:07.890
I can prefer chocolate over vanilla,

784
00:38:07.890 --> 00:38:10.993
but I can still have unconditional love for both flavors.

785
00:38:12.960 --> 00:38:17.510
Where do you feel judgment flaring up in yourself?

786
00:38:17.510 --> 00:38:18.963
Where are the challenges?

787
00:38:20.666 --> 00:38:22.420
Where do you draw the battle lines?

788
00:38:22.420 --> 00:38:26.140
Where's the evolution that you need

789
00:38:26.140 --> 00:38:29.187
to experience for yourself showing up in your life?

790
00:38:30.680 --> 00:38:33.350
Or are you just completely evolved at this point?

791
00:38:33.350 --> 00:38:38.190
No, I mean, one of my big woundings

792
00:38:38.190 --> 00:38:40.990
is being judged and marginalized

793
00:38:40.990 --> 00:38:42.660
for being a spiritual being

794
00:38:42.660 --> 00:38:44.940
with the awareness and perspective that I have.

795
00:38:44.940 --> 00:38:46.430
It's been painful.

796
00:38:46.430 --> 00:38:47.810
There's been times I haven't wanted

